WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.990 align:start position:0%
 
as the world continues to acknowledge  the power that anime and manga have on  modern pop culture we've begun to see  the amazing effects of this japanese  inspiration  other countries now create their own  animation series that even rival japan's  in entertainment quality as well as  other platforms and formats becoming not  necessarily a replacement but more so a  rapidly growing accompaniment to manga  and books and light novels for readers  across the world fervently seeking fresh  new content  with full color and a format easily  accessible from your phone or any device  you can mindlessly scroll through  webtoons are hard to ignore for manga  fans looking to expand their horizons  and admittedly i haven't dug my teeth as  far into webtoons as i would like to  aside from solo leveling god of high  school and tower of god my knowledge and  expertise in this area is quite notably  limited  but i will say that despite that i  believe that i can still recognize a  good promising series when it comes  around no matter what the format may be  the makings of a confident strong and  well-written protagonist  excellent world building that makes me  excited for the mystery and long journey  that is to come  and often a neglected trait of series  with powerful main characters a cast of  side characters that still feel fleshed  out and  honestly just relevant  i found all of this and more i believe  in doom breaker  a hot up-and-coming webtoon that has  reeled me in and genuinely engrossed me  in a way that few series do nowadays  zephyr is humanity's last and strongest  soldier we're thrown into the midst of  his lone battle against tartarus the god  of destruction and lord of demons the  one who took away his friends and  everyone he ever loved in the war  against the demons that has left zephyr  as the sole remnant of hope in this  feudal battle for what is now only a  memory of humankind  tartarus whether it be out of respect  for zephyr or as a final attempt to  humiliate him and laugh as he begs for a  chance to live offers humanity's  strongest soldier a chance to join him  and the demons  a chance for humans peak form to ascend  past his feeble frame  and as zephyr reaches out his hand to  the demon god she responds with exactly  what we would hope and expect of the  last human left  shaking tartarus's hand and triggering  his self-destruct spell  zephyr tells him  screw you [ __ ]  in his last moments though zephyr feels  regretful over his inability to avenge  those he lost he actually manages to  humiliate tartarus by injuring him for  the very first time in his eternal reign  as the god of destruction  it's a bitter defeat  and then he awakens  finding himself in the pantheon of the  gods zephyr is informed that at the  insistence of the gods themselves it has  been deemed that zephyr will be sent  back in time as a chance to change how  things ended  to erase this bitter defeat and replace  it hopefully with victory  though he will lose his physical  training mana and acquired skills he  will retain one thing  his memories and all of the knowledge he  has amassed throughout his life as the  most powerful human in the world  but zephyr isn't stupid it's something  you learn quite early on this isn't just  some checkpoint he can restart at some  perfect chance offered by the holy and  benevolent god above  when tartarus began slaughtering  humanity people's prayers to the gods  were ignored their offerings were  refused the priests who borrowed this  divine power originally were stripped of  it  the gods decided that humans no longer  had anything left to give and abandoned  them  so what reason could they have for  sending zephyr back in time  we want to see something  a little more entertaining  they enjoyed watching zephyr struggle  for years against the demons and were  saddened to see him die so soon they  even gave him a little help before he  died to try and keep him alive longer  for their entertainment like he was just  a play thing  which of course zephyr does not take  kindly to knowing that the lives of his  loved ones were nothing more than a show  for the god sitting idly by  even tartarus himself requested that  zephyr be sent back in time in order to  erase this humiliation from history's  record a petty act  but one that zephyr is fully ready to  take advantage  of given perks from the gods to support  him on his journey or rather make his  story a bit more fun in their eyes and  with the knowledge he's amassed zephyr  gladly takes up the chance to rewrite  history and take vengeance upon tartarus  and the other spiteful gods watching his  story  on zephyr's journey we watch what is  basically the epitome of someone  replaying a video game they've already  done a 100 walkthrough on before  having insight on how to quickly gain  power and the quickest methods to level  up on the early stages revealing and  utilizing information on enemies who  zeffer already knows details about half  of his conversations with new enemies  start with how do you know that  after zephyr reveals some piece of  information that no one in the world  would ever know  and while you think this might get old  the part that makes doom breaker great  is more so seeing how zephyr deviates  from what is essentially the original  story  zephyr is on a mission  everything he does has a purpose in the  long run to change the future  and his plans to befriend and meet  certain people from his past life come  with challenges but with his knowledge  of who they are and their stories he's  able to do it  he's essentially preparing humanity and  the people he knows for the danger and  war that lies ahead maybe even prevent  it he might be able to break free of the  doomed fate that lies in store for him  and the rest of humanity  in spite of how cheesy it might get i'm  a sucker for series with really  overpowered main protagonists  they tend to have a lot of problems  don't get me wrong it's something i  generally coin as the opmc dilemma a  poorly explored supporting cast a  shallow main character who fails to show  much growth over the course of the  series  villains who don't get a chance to shine  because they're quickly dismantled by  the protagonist  most series with an obviously  overpowered main character are  susceptible to at least a couple of  these issues  a good example lies with the later  stages of dragon ball z  during the buu arc the series begins to  disregard its side cast giving gohan  goten and trunks  massive power upgrades that were  immediately disregarded and used as  power upgrades for an antagonist whose  only trait was being an adaptive pink  alien who couldn't speak  leaving goku as the sole star of the  show and giving him super saiyan 3 a  power-up that held no emotional or plot  value like super saiyan 1 and super  saiyan 2 did except to simply be strong  to fight majin buu  but many series handle this dilemma  excellently and actually use it to their  advantage  one punch man avoided the issue of a  character who shows no development by  well embracing it  having the most simplistic funny main  character in both name and ability he is  exactly what you call him  mobscycle 100 has full fleshed out arcs  for many of its side characters avoiding  that issue of a weak supporting cast  many of whom have actually become fan  favorites in the series like regan  likewise doombreaker handles the issue  very well  zephyr is physically overpowered but not  grossly so  because he restarts with no skills or  mana except for the abilities given to  him by the gods he does have to continue  getting stronger through the story  he experiences many roadblocks hindering  his abilities early in the series as he  comes to terms with a body that is far  weaker than the one he used to have  but what sets this series apart from  most is that zephyr is insanely  overpowered not so much so in physical  abilities but in his knowledge  the true nature of most of the  characters in the story lets him  manipulate the tale to his will and the  location or method of gaining abilities  gives him the strength he needs to back  it  more than anything being physically  strong is just a way to support his  overarching plans rather than being  zephyr's biggest asset  he's a smart strong and scheming main  protagonist who you can't help but be  entranced by  and if you couldn't tell from the panels  i've been using the art is amazing  there's something utterly addicting  about reading through webtoons i'm not  sure if because of the simple top to  bottom format that it feels so easily  digestible or if the series is simply  that intriguing or both  i caught up with this series and was  genuinely ready to pay on the webtoon  app to read the extra five chapters once  i got there i think that doom breaker is  going to big places and i can't wait for  every single chapter that comes out  weekly  i highly recommend it  as always this has been the anime  culture corner i hope you enjoyed the  video don't forget to like and subscribe  for future in-depth show manga and  character analyses  you

